  "caption": "A cassette-shaped tape can now store data as synthetic DNA instead of magnetized sound.\n\nIn a reported ~100-meter length, researchers at Southern University of Science and Technology describe ~36 petabytes of capacity\u2014on the order of billions of songs.\n\nThe strangest part isn\u2019t the DNA, but the library system: microscopic barcodes point to where each file lives so retrieval doesn\u2019t require reading the entire archive.\n\nThe story unfolds slide by slide.\n\n#TheBoldUnknown #TheUnknownExplained #Curiosity #ScienceAndSociety #TechnologyAndCulture #EmergingTech #FutureTechnology #Biotechnology #DataStorage #DNADataStorage #SyntheticBiology",
